1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,824
Chai Corner now has five
outlets and thirty people.

2
00:00:04,124 --> 00:00:06,791
And all thirty still
report straight to Ravi.

3
00:00:07,341 --> 00:00:10,806
A new helper at outlet four
waits two days for an answer.

4
00:00:11,107 --> 00:00:14,762
A cash mistake at outlet two
goes unnoticed for a week.

5
00:00:15,062 --> 00:00:18,284
Ravi works late every night,
and still falls behind.

6
00:00:18,934 --> 00:00:21,071
Nobody can watch thirty people.

7
00:00:21,071 --> 00:00:22,700
His span is too wide.

8
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:25,231
So, what is span of control?

9
00:00:25,531 --> 00:00:30,058
Span of control, or span of management,
is how many people one manager

10
00:00:30,058 --> 00:00:31,437
can supervise well.

11
00:00:31,787 --> 00:00:35,133
Right now, Ravi's span is
thirty, with only two levels.

12
00:00:35,783 --> 00:00:40,062
So Ravi gives every outlet a
manager, like Meena at the bus stand.

13
00:00:40,412 --> 00:00:45,172
Now Ravi guides five outlet managers,
and each one guides five people.

14
00:00:45,522 --> 00:00:49,352
Same thirty people, but now
everyone has a boss close by.

15
00:00:50,002 --> 00:00:51,717
Now try a narrow span.

16
00:00:51,717 --> 00:00:54,221
Each manager guides just two people.

17
00:00:54,571 --> 00:00:57,573
That needs fifteen
managers, and five levels.

18
00:00:57,573 --> 00:00:59,104
The chart grows tall.

19
00:00:59,454 --> 00:01:00,437
Wide span.

20
00:01:00,437 --> 00:01:02,866
Each manager guides five people.

21
00:01:03,216 --> 00:01:05,979
Now just six managers, and three levels.

22
00:01:05,979 --> 00:01:07,366
The chart is flat.

23
00:01:08,016 --> 00:01:10,599
A tall structure gives close supervision.

24
00:01:10,599 --> 00:01:15,232
But messages pass slowly through every
level, and more managers cost more.

25
00:01:15,582 --> 00:01:18,680
A flat structure gives
freedom and fast messages.

26
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:23,094
But staff must be skilled, since
each boss has less time per person.

27
00:01:23,744 --> 00:01:26,227
The right span depends on five things.

28
00:01:26,677 --> 00:01:27,577
One.

29
00:01:27,234 --> 00:01:29,091
The nature of the work.

30
00:01:29,091 --> 00:01:31,504
Routine work allows a wide span.

31
00:01:31,504 --> 00:01:33,917
Complex work needs a narrow one.

32
00:01:34,267 --> 00:01:35,167
Two.

33
00:01:34,754 --> 00:01:37,314
The skill of the manager and the staff.

34
00:01:37,314 --> 00:01:39,272
Skilled people need less help.

35
00:01:39,622 --> 00:01:40,522
Three.

36
00:01:40,247 --> 00:01:42,030
The need for supervision.

37
00:01:42,030 --> 00:01:44,078
New staff need more guidance.

38
00:01:44,428 --> 00:01:45,328
Four.

39
00:01:45,048 --> 00:01:46,842
Communication technology.

40
00:01:46,842 --> 00:01:50,428
A phone group lets one
manager reach many people.

41
00:01:50,778 --> 00:01:51,718
And five.

42
00:01:51,718 --> 00:01:53,174
Geographic spread.

43
00:01:53,174 --> 00:01:56,820
People in faraway places
are harder to supervise.

44
00:01:57,470 --> 00:02:00,818
Chai work is routine, and
his managers are trained.

45
00:02:00,818 --> 00:02:02,823
So Ravi keeps the flat chart.

46
00:02:03,173 --> 00:02:07,072
Now a new helper gets an answer
in one hour, not two days.

47
00:02:07,072 --> 00:02:09,510
And Ravi talks to five, not thirty.

48
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:11,133
Quick check.

49
00:02:11,133 --> 00:02:14,114
Ravi wants faster messages
and fewer managers.

50
00:02:14,114 --> 00:02:15,760
Which should he choose?

51
00:02:17,660 --> 00:02:18,718
A wide span!

52
00:02:18,718 --> 00:02:22,662
Fewer levels, faster messages,
and fewer managers to pay.

53
00:02:23,262 --> 00:02:24,271
So, remember.

54
00:02:24,571 --> 00:02:29,040
Span of control is how many people
one manager can supervise well.

55
00:02:29,389 --> 00:02:31,746
A narrow span makes a tall structure.

56
00:02:31,746 --> 00:02:33,728
A wide span makes a flat one.

57
00:02:34,078 --> 00:02:38,356
The right span depends on the work,
the people, supervision, technology,

58
00:02:38,356 --> 00:02:39,283
and distance.

59
00:02:39,883 --> 00:02:41,901
Next time, the series finale.

60
00:02:41,901 --> 00:02:44,206
What makes an organization effective?
